# Design System (Tailwind CSS v4)

## Tokens over magic values

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<button className="rounded-cta bg-filled-dark px-6 py-2 text-filled-dark-fg">Confirmar</button>

// ❌ BAD
<button className="rounded-[26.5px] bg-[#041e41] px-6 py-2 text-[#ffffff]">Confirmar</button>
```

## Key files

- `apps/web/src/styles/tokens.css` — color/radius primitives as CSS variables
- `apps/web/src/styles/global.css` — semantic mapping + `@theme inline` Tailwind wiring
- `DESIGN.md` — agent-readable token mirror
- `knowledge/design-system.md` — usage rules

## Primary color rule — MANDATORY

> **Primary action color is navy (filled-dark), not blue.**

Primary CTAs: `bg-filled-dark` + `text-filled-dark-fg`.
Advisor send buttons: `bg-advisor-submit` + `text-advisor-submit-fg`.

## Only mapped tokens exist

`tokens.css` holds only the colors the app uses. A utility built from an unmapped primitive, such as `bg-gray-chat-bg`, renders nothing. To add a color: define the primitive in `tokens.css`, map it in `@theme inline` in `global.css`, then record it in `DESIGN.md`.

There is no accent blue and no dark mode. Add `brand-accent-50` (`#0431c0`) back when a screen needs links or brand accents.
